          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Recall that the absolute value function is defined by",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-q7-definition-math",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "|x|=\\begin{cases}-x,&x<0,\\\\x,&x\\ge0.\\end{cases}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $|x|=\\sqrt{x^2}$. Hint: Consider two cases: $x<0$ and $x\\ge0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$|x|=\\sqrt{x^2}$.\n\nFor $x<0$, both sides equal $-x$; for $x\\ge0$, both sides equal $x$.",
          "worked": "If $x<0$, then $-x>0$ and $|x|=-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x^2}&=\\sqrt{(-x)^2}\\\\\\sqrt{x^2}&=-x\\\\\\sqrt{x^2}&=|x|\\end{align*}$$\nIf $x\\ge0$, then $|x|=x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x^2}&=x\\\\\\sqrt{x^2}&=|x|\\end{align*}$$\nThus $|x|=\\sqrt{x^2}$ in both cases.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-bc-group",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p7-q7-bc-instruction-paragraph",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Use part (a) to prove each of the following:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p7-q7-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$|xy|=|x||y|$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$|xy|=|x||y|$.\n\nUse part (a) to equate the squares, then take non-negative square roots.",
              "worked": "Using part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}|xy|^2&=(xy)^2\\\\|xy|^2&=x^2y^2\\\\|xy|^2&=|x|^2|y|^2\\\\|xy|^2&=(|x||y|)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $|xy|$ and $|x||y|$ are non-negative, so $|xy|=|x||y|$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 30
          },
          {
            "id": "p7-q7-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\left|\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right|=\\dfrac{|x|}{|y|}$ given $y\\ne0$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\left|\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right|=\\dfrac{|x|}{|y|}$ for $y\\ne0$.\n\nUse part (a) to equate the squares, then take non-negative square roots.",
              "worked": "Using part (a), with $y\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left|\\frac{x}{y}\\right|^2&=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)^2\\\\\\left|\\frac{x}{y}\\right|^2&=\\frac{x^2}{y^2}\\\\\\left|\\frac{x}{y}\\right|^2&=\\frac{|x|^2}{|y|^2}\\\\\\left|\\frac{x}{y}\\right|^2&=\\left(\\frac{|x|}{|y|}\\right)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $|y|>0$, both quantities are non-negative. Hence $\\left|\\frac{x}{y}\\right|=\\frac{|x|}{|y|}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 38
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p7-q7-distance-paragraph",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The absolute value function is important as it is used to find the distance between two real numbers. That is, the distance between ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "x",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "y",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "|x-y|",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". For example, the distance between 2 and 7 is ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "|2-7|=|-5|=5",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p7-q7-d-task",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Prove that ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "|x-y|=|y-x|",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$|x-y|=|y-x|$.\n\nApply part (b) to $x-y=-(y-x)$.",
          "worked": "Using part (b),\n$$\\begin{align*}|x-y|&=|-(y-x)|\\\\|x-y|&=|-1||y-x|\\\\|x-y|&=|y-x|.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Prove the triangle inequality,\n$$|x+y|\\le|x|+|y|.$$\nHint: Begin by writing $|x+y|^2=(x+y)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$|x+y|\\le|x|+|y|$.\n\nUse $xy\\le|x||y|$ to compare squares, then take non-negative square roots.",
          "worked": "Since $xy\\le|xy|=|x||y|$, part (a) gives\n$$\\begin{align*}|x+y|^2&=(x+y)^2\\\\|x+y|^2&=x^2+2xy+y^2\\\\|x+y|^2&=|x|^2+2xy+|y|^2\\\\|x+y|^2&\\le|x|^2+2|x||y|+|y|^2\\\\|x+y|^2&\\le(|x|+|y|)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $|x+y|$ and $|x|+|y|$ are non-negative. Taking square roots gives $|x+y|\\le|x|+|y|$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-fg-group",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p7-q7-fg-instruction-paragraph",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The inequalities below are known as the ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "reverse triangle inequality",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". Use part (e) to prove these inequalities:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p7-q7-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "$|x-y|\\ge|x|-|y|$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$|x-y|\\ge|x|-|y|$.\n\nApply the triangle inequality to $x=(x-y)+y$ and subtract $|y|$.",
              "worked": "By part (e),\n$$\\begin{align*}|x|&=|(x-y)+y|\\\\|x|&\\le|x-y|+|y|.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting $|y|$ gives $|x|-|y|\\le|x-y|$, so $|x-y|\\ge|x|-|y|$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 27
          },
          {
            "id": "p7-q7-g",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "g",
            "prompt": "$|x-y|\\ge|y|-|x|$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$|x-y|\\ge|y|-|x|$.\n\nInterchange $x$ and $y$ in part (f), then use part (d).",
              "worked": "Interchanging $x$ and $y$ in part (f) gives\n$$|y-x|\\ge|y|-|x|.$$\nBy part (d), $|x-y|=|y-x|$. Hence\n$$|x-y|\\ge|y|-|x|.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
